# BeiDou B-CNAV 64-ary LDPC parity-check matrix definitions.
#
# Source of truth (transcribed from the official ICD PDFs, en.beidou.gov.cn):
#   - BDS-SIS-ICD-B1C-1.0 (2017-12) §6.2.2.2: H100,200 (B-CNAV1 subframe 2)
#     and §6.2.2.3: H44,88 (B-CNAV1 subframe 3)
#   - BDS-SIS-ICD-B2a-1.0 (2017-12) §6.2.2: H48,96 (B-CNAV2)
#   - BDS-SIS-ICD-B2b-1.0 (2020-07) §6.2.2: H81,162 (B-CNAV3)
#
# Each code is a (2,4)-regular non-binary LDPC code over GF(2^6) with
# primitive polynomial p(x) = 1 + x + x^6 (ICD convention; symbols map to
# bits MSB first, so symbol value 1 is the bit vector 000001). Every check
# row has exactly four non-zero entries; `index[i]` holds their 0-based
# column positions (ascending, as printed in the ICD) and `element[i]` the
# GF(2^6) values at those positions, both for check row i (0-based). The
# first k columns are the information symbols and the last n-k columns the
# parity symbols (H is systematic-ready: its parity part is invertible).
#
# The ICD prints each table as four column groups read top-to-bottom then
# left-to-right (ICD "reading flow chart" figures); the tuples below are in
# plain row order i = 0 .. n-k-1. Committed so `generate_beidou_alist.jl`
# can reproduce `data/bcnv*.alist` with no external dependency.

